  "result": "I've written the plan to `<home>\\.claude\\plans\\add-a-new-parameter-glowing-goblet.md`. I haven't changed any code, because plan mode is still on. `ExitPlanMode` isn't available in this session, so I can't request approval the normal way.\n\n**Plan**\n- **Type:** add `class KeyValue(ParamType[tuple[str, str]])` in `src/click/types.py`, modeled on `UUIDParameterType`.\n  - It splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` gives `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`, and `a=` is allowed with an empty value.\n  - Input with no `=`, or with an empty key, calls `self.fail(\"{value!r} is not a valid key=value pair.\")`, so it raises `BadParameter`.\n  - A tuple that is already converted passes through unchanged.\n  - The metavar is `KEY=VALUE`.\n- **Export:** add `from .types import KeyValue as KeyValue` to `src/click/__init__.py`.\n- **Docs:** add entries in `docs/api.md`, `docs/parameter-types.md` and `CHANGES.md`.\n- **Tests:** add valid and invalid cases and an end-to-end `CliRunner` test in `tests/test_types.py`. Add a `KeyValue` entry to the parametrized list in `tests/test_info_dict.py`.\n- **Verification:** run pytest, run the type checker if one is configured, and try `--set a=b`, `--set a` and `--set =b` by hand.\n\nReply to approve the plan and I'll implement it.",
